const hreflang = "<link rel='alternate' hreflang='en' href='https://cholinebio.com/feed-additives-classification/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='x-default' href='https://cholinebio.com/feed-additives-classification/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='ar' href='https://cholinebio.com/ar/%d8%aa%d8%b5%d9%86%d9%8a%d9%81-%d8%a5%d8%b6%d8%a7%d9%81%d8%a7%d8%aa-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%a3%d8%b9%d9%84%d8%a7%d9%81-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%85%d8%b6%d8%a7%d9%81%d8%a9/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='fr' href='https://cholinebio.com/fr/classification-des-additifs-pour-lalimentation-animale/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='tr' href='https://cholinebio.com/tr/yem-katki-maddeleri%cc%87-siniflandirmasi/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='es' href='https://cholinebio.com/es/clasificacion-de-los-aditivos-para-piensos/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='de' href='https://cholinebio.com/de/klassifizierung-von-futtermittelzusatzstoffen/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='zh' href='https://cholinebio.com/zh/%e9%a5%b2%e6%96%99%e6%b7%bb%e5%8a%a0%e5%89%82%e5%88%86%e7%b1%bb/'/><link rel='alternate' hreflang='pt' href='https://cholinebio.com/pt/classificacao-dos-aditivos-para-racoes/'/>";
---
<BaseLayout title={page.title} ogType="website" canonical="/feed-additives-classification/" hreflang={hreflang}>
  <article class="page-content">
    <h1 class="page-title">{page.h1}</h1>
    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<header class="entry-header page-title title-align-inherit title-tablet-align-inherit title-mobile-align-inherit"><h1 class="entry-title">Feed Additives Classification — Dinweys Biotech</h1><nav id="kadence-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumbs"  class="kadence-breadcrumbs"><div class="kadence-breadcrumb-container"><span><a href="/" itemprop="url" class="kadence-bc-home" ><span>Home</span></a></span> <span class="bc-delimiter">/</span> <span class="kadence-bread-current">Feed Additives Classification — Dinweys Biotech</span></div></nav></header><div class="entry-content single-content"><div class="kb-row-layout-wrap kb-row-layout-id503_3cf99a-55 alignnone wp-block-kadence-rowlayout"><div class="kt-row-column-wrap kt-has-1-columns kt-row-layout-equal kt-tab-layout-inherit kt-mobile-layout-row kt-row-valign-top kb-theme-content-width"><div class="wp-block-kadence-column kadence-column503_1d5e3e-64"><div class="kt-inside-inner-col"><h1 class="kt-adv-heading503_d4093a-75 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading" data-kb-block="kb-adv-heading503_d4093a-75">Feed Additives Classification — Dinweys Biotech Product Guide</h1><p><a href="/product/" data-internallinksmanager029f6b8e52c="4" title="Feed additives">Feed additives</a> are essential ingredients in modern animal nutrition, categorized by their function, composition, and regulatory status. Dinweys Biotech provides a comprehensive range of feed additives sourced from leading Chinese manufacturers. This guide explains the classification system and helps buyers understand the product categories available for global distribution.</p></div></div></div></div><h2>Nutritional Feed Additives</h2><h3>Amino Acids</h3><p>Amino acids are the building blocks of protein. Essential amino acids cannot be synthesized by animals in sufficient quantities and must be supplied through feed. Key products include:</p><ul><li><strong>L-Lysine Sulphate 70%</strong> — Essential for swine and poultry growth. Lysine is typically the first limiting amino acid in corn-soy diets.</li><li><strong>DL-Methionine</strong> — Crucial for feather development in poultry and immune function across species.</li><li><strong>L-Threonine</strong> — Supports gut health and mucin production, particularly in young animals.</li></ul><h3>Vitamins</h3><p><a href="/product_category/vitamins/" data-internallinksmanager029f6b8e52c="2" title="vitamins">Vitamin</a> supplements ensure animals receive adequate micronutrients for metabolic function. Dinweys Biotech supplies:</p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin B2 (Riboflavin)</strong> — 80% feed grade, essential for energy metabolism</li><li><strong>Vitamin C (Ascorbic Acid)</strong> — Supports immune function, particularly during heat stress</li><li><strong><a href="/product/choline-chloride-60/" data-internallinksmanager029f6b8e52c="1" title="Choline Chloride 60% Feed Additive – Corn Cob Carrier China Manufacturer Supply">Choline Chloride</a></strong> — 60% and 50% corn cob carrier; 75% liquid. Essential for lipid metabolism, liver function, and growth performance</li></ul><h3>Minerals</h3><ul><li><strong><a href="/product/dcp-dicalcium-phosphate-17/" data-internallinksmanager029f6b8e52c="5" title="DCP17">Dicalcium Phosphate</a> (DCP)</strong> — 17% and 18% phosphorus grades. Combined with calcium for skeletal development in growing animals and laying hens.</li><li><strong>Betaine HCl</strong> — 96% and 98% purity. Acts as a methyl donor, supports osmotic regulation, and improves carcass quality in swine.</li><li><strong>Betaine Anhydrous</strong> — Concentrated form for high-inclusion formulations.</li></ul><h2>Functional Feed Additives</h2><h3>Enzymes</h3><p>Feed enzymes improve nutrient digestibility and reduce feed costs:</p><ul><li><strong>Phytase</strong> — Heat-stable and granular forms. Releases bound phosphorus from plant-based feed ingredients, reducing the need for inorganic phosphate supplementation</li><li><strong>Carbohydrases</strong> — Break down non-starch polysaccharides to improve energy utilization</li></ul><h3>Phytogenic Additives</h3><p>Plant-derived compounds including essential oils, herbs, spices, and extracts. Used as natural growth promoters and alternatives to antibiotic growth promoters.</p><h2>Regulatory Classification</h2><p>Feed additives are regulated differently across regions. Dinweys Biotech supports compliance with:</p><ul><li><strong>EU Regulations</strong> — EC 1831/2003 classification system</li><li><strong>FDA/AAFCO</strong> — US regulatory framework</li><li><strong>China GB Standards</strong> — Domestic Chinese feed additive regulations</li><li><strong>COSUC / ANVISA</strong> — Latin American market requirements</li></ul><p>For detailed product specifications, pricing, and documentation, <a href="/contact/">contact the Dinweys Biotech team</a>.</p></div>`} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
